Hello 3Dnatives team,

a pitch with a detail that may matter for your multilingual editions:
Solidon3D ships its interface and its complete manual in six languages —
German, English, Spanish, French, Italian and Portuguese. Not a machine
translation of the menus, but the manual as well.

The product: a desktop application that takes downloaded 3D models and makes
their features editable without CAD knowledge. Move a hole, change a
countersink, add a thread that fits.

Version 0.5.0 is the largest step so far. Until now the result of an edit was
a triangle mesh; now it is an exact body. Primitives are built with real faces
and edges, and holes, slots, countersinks, bosses, beads, grooves and threads
stay exact when they are moved, duplicated, rotated or removed. STEP goes in
and comes back out cleanly. Two geometry kernels run under one interface and
the options that used to switch between them are gone — the software keeps the
exact body where it can and names the limit where it cannot.

The most visual addition: a honeycomb pattern, knurl, set of ribs, waves or
knobs is recognised as one feature with pitch, cell width and depth instead of
hundreds of faces. One click removes it, three numbers set it again, including
around a handle — a texture on a cylinder follows the curvature, so the
grooves are equally deep everywhere and the pattern closes without a seam.

Also: dimensions are edited directly on the model with a live preview; resin
printers are supported with pixel size and minimum wall; a model with open
areas is closed while it is read; and recognition is several times faster.

70 user-visible changes in this release; 896 since the first 0.1 demo.

Licensing is a one-time purchase in three tiers, with no subscription. After a
single activation the application runs fully offline, with no account and no
telemetry.

Solidon3D is a desktop application for Windows, macOS and Linux. One-time
purchase, no subscription, no account: after a single activation it runs fully
offline. Interface and manual are available in six languages, and there is a
demo.

I am happy to provide a review licence, print-resolution images or answers to
any question directly.

